{
  "id": 299923603,
  "iid": 15523,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Zigbee ZCL: OTA Upgrade Time can be UTC not offset time",
  "description": "According to ZCL v8, 11.11.4 https://zigbeealliance.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/07-5123-08-Zigbee-Cluster-Library.pdf, Table 11-15,\n\ninside `Upgrade Response End` command, `Upgrade Time` field contains either offset time (e.g. upgrade after 60 seconds) or UTC time (i.e. upgrade at this specific time).\n\nBut currently it is always displayed as offset (aka relative) time, this sometimes results in the following obscured values:\n```\nCurrent Time: May  2, 2024 18:04:21 West Asia Standard Time \nUpgrade Time: 8888 days, 13 hours, 4 minutes, 21 seconds from now\n```\n\nThe spec says that it is UTC time when `Current Time` field is not `0x00000000`, which is used by OTA server that cannot put time values in timestamps. OTA client always might know offset time by subtracting `Current Time` from `Upgrade Time`.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2024-05-04T18:40:56.052Z",
  "updated_at": "2024-05-07T14:16:55.840Z",
